<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en-GB"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Model-risk crosswalk for a vendor credit score</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">
<style>
@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm 11mm; }
body { font-family: Inter, "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif; color:#111; font-size:7.3pt; line-height:1.32; margin:0; }
h1 { font-family:"Instrument Serif", Georgia, serif; font-weight:400; font-size:20pt; line-height:1; margin:0 0 4px; } .sub { color:#6b6b6b; font-size:7.4pt; margin-bottom:7px; }
table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; border-top:1px solid #111; } th { background:none; color:#6b6b6b; font-family:"Geist Mono", monospace; font-size:6pt; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase; text-align:left; padding:4px 4px 3px; font-weight:400; border-bottom:1px solid #dcdcdc; }
td { padding:2.6px 4px; border-bottom:1px solid #e3e3e3; vertical-align:top; }
.core { font-family:"Geist Mono", monospace; font-size:5.8pt; letter-spacing:.06em; color:#111; border:1px solid #111; padding:0 2px; } .foot { color:#6b6b6b; font-size:6.6pt; margin-top:5px; border-top:1px solid #111; padding-top:4px; }
</style></head><body>
<h1>Model-risk crosswalk: what to demand from a credit-score vendor</h1>
<div class="sub">One page from the Third-Party Model Review (public-evidence review, 12 Nov 2026). SR 26-2 (17 Apr 2026, superseding SR 11-7), PRA SS1/23 principles P1 to P5, EBA GL/2020/06 s4.3.4, MaRisk (Circular 06/2026) and the AI Act as amended by Reg (EU) 2026/1744. Status column: what the public record shows for {{ v.score_name }}.</div>
<table><thead><tr><th style="width:3%">El.</th><th style="width:12%">Element</th><th style="width:20%">Anchors</th><th style="width:30%">Evidence a lender should hold</th><th style="width:14%">Public status ({{ v.vendor }})</th><th style="width:21%">Request</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in crosswalk %}<tr><td><b>{{ r.element }}</b></td><td>{{ r.name }}{% if r.core %} <span class="core">CORE</span>{% endif %}</td><td>{{ r.anchors }}</td><td>{{ s(r.expected) }}</td><td>{{ r.status.value }}{% if not r.ratable %} <b>(not ratable)</b>{% endif %}</td>{% set ns = namespace(r=[]) %}{% for f in findings if f.id in r.findings %}{% for q in f.requests %}{% if q not in ns.r %}{% set ns.r = ns.r + [q] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}<td>{{ ns.r|join(', ') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<div class="foot">Prepared by Fiona Edocket as a portfolio case study; Mainkai Direktbank AG is fictional. Not an audit, validation or legal opinion. Request numbers refer to the evidence request (E01 to E14) in the review. ECB guide to internal models: not applied, as it covers IRB internal models, which are out of scope. Its machine-learning section (explainability, and performance that justifies complexity) is used only as a reference point for elements D and G.</div>
</body></html>
